      "description": "Building on the knowledge acquired in ARAB1000, this course aims to further develop students’ ability to communicate in Arabic in various everyday situations. It also seeks to give students a taste of Arabic culture and invites them to explore cultural differences. Through intensive practice students will develop more confidence in interacting in Arabic while further expanding and solidifying their understanding of the basic grammar and pronunciation patterns.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "Prerequisite: ARAB1000\nNot for students who have taken ARAB2001,2050,3000 or 3050",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Classwork",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "academic_org": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "learning_outcomes": "Upon successful completion of the course, students will have acquired the ability to:\n• read Arabic texts containing high frequency lexis and basic structures;\n• understand basic conversations or understand the gist of more complex conversations dealing with familiar topics;\n• talk on familiar and simple topics with reasonable fluency;\n• ask for information, make suggestions and make requests fairly confidently;\n• write a short personal text or letter about familiar subjects.\nBy the end of the course, students should be able to perform at Level A1.2 of the Common European Framework.",
